# Environment file for fim-agent.service (D36/RN-130).
#
# `agent/install.sh` generates /etc/fim-agent/env automatically (D56/RN-150,
# design D-7 of vps-deployment-readiness): `agent/installer.py apply` reads
# the bootstrap secret ONLY from a hidden prompt or --bootstrap-secret-file
# (never from a flag, and never from an environment variable — the secret
# itself is never accepted as installer input by name) and writes it here as
# `FIM_BOOTSTRAP_SECRET=<secret>`, with mode 0600 owned by root:root —
# systemd reads EnvironmentFile= as root before dropping privileges, so the
# service user never needs read access to it. It never overwrites an
# existing env file unless invoked with --reconfigure. This file exists only
# as a reference for a manual install outside install.sh; the installer never
# copies it verbatim.
#
# FIM_BOOTSTRAP_SECRET is required only for the agent's FIRST boot on a host
# with no valid certificate yet (see agent/__main__.py, agent/bootstrap.py).
# It is single-use: once bootstrap succeeds the agent holds a certificate and
# never reads this value again. For a manual install, uncomment, set it,
# start the service once, then remove the line (or delete the file) — the
# unit declares `EnvironmentFile=-/etc/fim-agent/env` (leading dash), so a
# missing file never prevents startup after bootstrap.

#FIM_BOOTSTRAP_SECRET=
